  "section_notes": "S1 requires fast reporting (24h) and customer notice (72h) for all incidents. S2 keeps the 5% limit but allows up to 24 months for existing models with a risk-based corrective plan and no automatic sales stop; per-model results go to customers but not the public. S3 mandates new-unit shut-off from adoption and a 6-year retrofit with a feasibility escape. S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months. S5 makes recall mandatory at 8/100k with immediate notices."
